Package: irxclean
Type: Package
Title: Model-Informed Detection of Potentially Erroneous Pharmacokinetic Observations
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("InsightRX", role = "cph"),
    person("Jordan Brooks", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "jordan.brooks@insight-rx.com")
  )
Description: Provides tools for flagging potentially erroneous pharmacokinetic
    observations in clinical data for user investigation and review, using
    model-informed iterative approaches. Includes functionality for gross data
    quality assessment (covariate distribution outlier detection, concentration
    anomalies), model-dependent iterative flagging based on conditional weighted
    residuals (CWRES) via Perl-speaks-NONMEM (PsN) or the ferx estimation
    engine, model stability monitoring
    across iterations, and demographic comparison of subjects with flagged
    observations versus the full dataset. An automated report can be generated
    summarising all findings. Final exclusion decisions remain with the user
    after reviewing flagged observations.
